menu "RW1 AI Interaction (board to PC server)"

    # WiFi 凭据与服务器地址**刻意不在这里**（2026-09-23 决定）。
    #
    # 它们原来叫 RW1_WIFI_SSID / RW1_WIFI_PASSWORD / RW1_SERVER_URL，编译期烧进固件。
    # 两个问题：
    #   1. 把固件发给别人 = 把自己的 WiFi 密码一起发出去；
    #   2. "老 sdkconfig 一字不改仍然能跑"这句承诺在实机上不成立 ——
    #      net_config_present() 只看 NVS，NVS 空就进配网，根本走不到 Kconfig 回退那条路。
    #
    # 现在**配网是唯一入口**（双击 BOOT 进 AP → 手机上填表 → 存 NVS）。
    # 于是固件里永远不可能包含 WiFi 密码。要改网络/服务器地址也不用重编译。
    # 详见 README「运行期配置：SoftAP 配网」与 PROPOSAL §1.8。

    config RW1_WIFI_MAX_RETRY
        int "Maximum connection retries"
        default 8

    config RW1_TELEMETRY_PERIOD_MS
        int "Telemetry period (ms)"
        default 500
        help
            How often the board POSTs one batch of buffered IMU samples to
            the server. Keep this well above RW1_SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS.

    config RW1_SAMPLE_PERIOD_MS
        int "IMU sampling period (ms)"
        default 10
        help
            10 ms = 100 Hz. Samples are buffered locally and sent as a single
            batch every RW1_TELEMETRY_PERIOD_MS, so the HTTP rate stays low
            while the server still gets a real waveform.

            Do not raise this above ~20 ms: step counting (walking is
            1.5-2.5 Hz) and free-fall detection (< 0.5 s of weightlessness)
            are physically impossible below 50 Hz. The original 500 ms
            (2 Hz) sampling made both features silently fake.

    config RW1_IMU_DEBUG_LOG
        bool "Periodic IMU diagnostic log (1 Hz)"
        default y
        help
            Once per second the transport task logs one line with the raw
            sensor sample, the screen-frame values, |a| and the active
            orientation. Used to validate the sensor->screen axis mapping
            on a real board: hold the board in a known pose and compare
            against the expected numbers.

            Expected values (screen frame: +x right, +y down, +z out of
            the screen): flat on table, screen up -> (0, 0, +1);
            standing on the top edge -> y = -1; bottom edge -> y = +1;
            right edge -> x = +1; left edge -> x = -1. |a| should read
            ~1.00 g whenever the board is at rest.

            Turn it off to reduce log noise once the mapping is confirmed.

    config RW1_CAMERA_SELFTEST
        bool "Camera self-test at boot (capture one frame, then release)"
        default y
        help
            On boot, start the on-board OV2640, capture a single JPEG frame,
            log its resolution / byte count / JPEG marker validity, then shut
            the camera down again.

            It releases the camera afterwards on purpose: keeping the DVP
            interface streaming would compete with LVGL refresh and IMU
            telemetry for memory bandwidth. The point is to prove the
            hardware and the Kconfig flags are right -- the actual "capture
            on demand" feature (weeks 7-9) will call camera_init() again
            when a photo is requested.

            Requires CONFIG_CAMERA_OV2640 and a JPEG format entry, both of
            which are set in sdkconfig.bsp.esp32_s3_eye. Failure here never
            blocks boot; it only logs an error.

endmenu
